Found under k315 (2026-10-31). lib/OCP/Cmd/Destroy.pm ~399 reads a worker pool's nodes the way Apply/CR.pm worker_ocpnodes does, and `ocp destroy` runs no validate(): an ssh pool with a boolean entry dies inside Perl ("Not a HASH reference"), a hetzner pool with a list there numifies it. k315 refuses those shapes in validate(), but destroy never asks.

Fix: run validate() (or the pool-nodes part, Config::_pool_nodes_errors) before destroy reads the pools, and stop with its lines on STDERR; or read through the same helper. Related: k306 (commands that read control_planes/workers without validate()).

Done = `ocp destroy` on a malformed pool nodes: stops with validate()'s line before it deletes anything (test).

